WEBVTT

01:01.561 --> 01:03.772
100 YEARS OF MODERN METEOROLOGY
NEW CHALLENGES

01:11.821 --> 01:13.490
Relationships evolve.

01:19.746 --> 01:22.707
It can make them stronger
or make them fall apart.

01:23.666 --> 01:25.919
The changes depend on time.

01:27.170 --> 01:31.966
And how each person's emotions build,
with or against their partner.

01:35.220 --> 01:37.347
- Mm, we need the food too.
- Oh!

01:37.430 --> 01:39.224
- Like that?
- Ah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:52.445 --> 01:53.863
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:53.947 --> 01:57.784
we are beginning our descent
to Jeju International Airport.

01:57.867 --> 02:01.579
Please fasten your seatbelts
and open the shade to your windows.

02:01.663 --> 02:02.831
Thank you.

02:08.378 --> 02:09.796
What's scary is…

02:10.588 --> 02:12.715
I want things to work out.

02:14.801 --> 02:17.554
I want things to work out
for the two of us.

02:18.429 --> 02:19.556
But…

02:21.432 --> 02:23.226
that's the only thing.

02:25.770 --> 02:30.608
Although that stays under control
with tempered feelings.

02:30.692 --> 02:33.027
I like it simple and stable.

02:34.571 --> 02:37.115
If things start to go beyond moderate,

02:38.867 --> 02:40.368
I become anxious.

02:43.872 --> 02:45.290
Then I feel…

02:46.457 --> 02:48.626
I become someone else and not myself.

02:54.090 --> 02:55.800
Get up. Let's take you back home.

02:56.968 --> 02:58.803
So then you should decide.

03:00.346 --> 03:02.765
You should decide while you're in Jeju.

03:07.937 --> 03:11.232
If you think you can do it moderately

03:11.316 --> 03:12.942
or not.

03:13.026 --> 03:15.486
Really think about it, then decide.

03:20.241 --> 03:23.328
Knowing little misunderstandings
and disagreements

03:23.953 --> 03:27.165
pushed the evolution,
and we don't notice it.

03:28.166 --> 03:31.294
And we can fall
out of sync with each other.

03:32.879 --> 03:36.132
All I really wanted was a moment.

03:36.966 --> 03:38.301
Like this.

03:39.469 --> 03:42.472
To have time to realign and be together.

04:00.114 --> 04:03.326
I must have missed
where we fell out.

04:05.870 --> 04:11.334
How did we end up looking down a path

04:12.377 --> 04:16.214
with no idea of what awaits us?

04:22.971 --> 04:26.432
EPISODE 12
VARIATION AREA

04:26.516 --> 04:30.812
WHEN A HOT TYPHOON CHANGES
AS IT PASSES THROUGH KOREA'S COLD AIR

04:30.895 --> 04:34.774
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

04:44.200 --> 04:46.077
Thank you.

04:50.373 --> 04:52.750
I didn't realize you are so invested.

04:53.418 --> 04:54.877
Who knows what I feel?

04:55.628 --> 04:58.214
It seems like everything is falling apart.

05:07.932 --> 05:10.601
Director! Where's your phone?
We've been calling you.

05:10.685 --> 05:12.937
- We couldn't reach you.
- Is there something wrong?

05:13.855 --> 05:15.606
The Situation Room is in chaos.

05:15.690 --> 05:17.108
You have to go right now.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.945
I want to talk to the guy in charge.

05:21.529 --> 05:23.656
Damn it, bring me your boss, okay?

05:23.740 --> 05:25.658
- Don't you film this!
- Okay, okay, we understand.

05:25.742 --> 05:26.951
I need you to calm down.

05:27.035 --> 05:28.703
You can talk to someone outside.

05:28.786 --> 05:31.748
Outside? You think I can calm down
and leave right now

05:31.831 --> 05:34.876
when my only kid's bleeding out
in the hospital somewhere?

05:34.959 --> 05:37.587
No information. He's dead for all I know!

05:37.670 --> 05:40.673
I'm worried out of my mind,
and you say, "Just calm down"?

05:41.257 --> 05:44.302
For Christ's sake! Is this funny?
Is this a joke to you?

05:44.385 --> 05:45.887
I can't calm down!

05:45.970 --> 05:47.972
How will what you're doing help your son?

05:48.056 --> 05:49.849
What? Are you the boss man?

05:49.932 --> 05:51.392
Huh? Back off.

05:51.476 --> 05:53.436
- Back off!
- What's going on?

05:56.022 --> 05:57.982
Oh. It's you.

05:59.067 --> 06:00.943
I'm Director Jin Ha-kyung of Team Two.

06:01.027 --> 06:02.487
I'm Mr. Lee's supervisor.

06:02.570 --> 06:04.322
Right. Director Lady.

06:05.448 --> 06:08.076
You hear what happened?
They let my boy get hurt.

06:08.910 --> 06:09.911
Yes.

06:09.994 --> 06:13.122
Someone from Jeju called
and said he's in the hospital.

06:13.206 --> 06:16.459
I couldn't breathe.
My heart was gonna beat out of my chest.

06:16.542 --> 06:18.753
I couldn't see. I blacked out!

06:18.836 --> 06:20.880
I can discuss it with you outside of here.

06:20.963 --> 06:23.132
We don't allow civilians
in the Situation Room.

06:23.216 --> 06:24.258
For real?

06:24.342 --> 06:25.802
Finally, please get him out.

06:25.885 --> 06:27.929
- Come here, man.
- Shit. Stay away.

06:28.012 --> 06:29.972
You want some of this? You can't touch me!

06:30.056 --> 06:32.392
Don't try it! Just stay away!

06:34.560 --> 06:36.604
I have rights. Don't touch me.

06:36.687 --> 06:38.439
You're attacking me!

06:38.523 --> 06:40.108
I'll sue everyone here!

06:43.486 --> 06:44.529
I got it.

06:45.279 --> 06:46.322
Hello, sir.

06:47.323 --> 06:49.367
What you're doing
is obstructing official duties.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.369
What, so?

06:51.452 --> 06:52.703
Are you going to sue me, then?

06:52.787 --> 06:54.580
I'm just trying to explain to you

06:54.664 --> 06:56.666
that it's important
that they can do their work.

06:56.749 --> 06:59.710
It's not the place to show up
and make demands. Understand?

06:59.794 --> 07:01.587
- Hey!
- Okay, you can talk to me.

07:01.671 --> 07:03.172
My boy is important, too.

07:03.256 --> 07:05.341
He's the only son
for two generations in a row.

07:05.425 --> 07:06.884
He's all I got!

07:06.968 --> 07:08.261
Damn it.

07:12.598 --> 07:14.183
Our Lady Director knows best.

07:14.267 --> 07:17.186
You personally know my son's important.

07:17.270 --> 07:18.438
You're close, right?

07:26.195 --> 07:29.657
I'm referring to seeing you and my son

07:29.740 --> 07:32.452
being close enough
to hit the motel together.

07:37.498 --> 07:38.416
Ah.

07:38.499 --> 07:40.585
I see. No one knows.

07:42.044 --> 07:43.463
Okay, okay, I get it.

07:43.546 --> 07:45.631
I won't talk too loud.

07:48.342 --> 07:53.347
Anyway, it's true that… that you two
are in a relationship, then?

07:58.436 --> 08:00.521
Well, I know what I saw in that motel.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.942
You guys see each other, right?

08:09.489 --> 08:10.781
That's enough.

08:12.366 --> 08:13.910
What, she's got nothing to say?

08:15.828 --> 08:17.872
We're going outside.
We'll talk there, okay?

08:22.418 --> 08:23.294
Sure, let's go.

08:23.920 --> 08:25.463
We've got lots to discuss.

08:35.556 --> 08:38.184
I can handle this.
Don't feel like you have to be there.

08:51.781 --> 08:52.657
Oh.

09:14.595 --> 09:16.556
- Mr. Um.
- Hm?

09:19.642 --> 09:21.269
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

09:21.352 --> 09:23.980
Wow, when did that start, huh?

09:31.821 --> 09:33.990
Hello. Headquarters. This is Um.

09:34.073 --> 09:35.449
We just saw it.

09:36.075 --> 09:37.410
Is it a…

09:37.493 --> 09:41.289
Typhoon, yes. Number 15 Elisha,
that was following Number 14 Ricky.

09:41.372 --> 09:45.501
Around eleven o'clock today,
it was moving northeastward,

09:45.585 --> 09:48.671
300km near Okinawa,
the central pressure was 990,

09:48.754 --> 09:51.799
max wind velocity, 20 per second,
and a radius of 150.

10:05.688 --> 10:07.023
You have a cig?

10:09.150 --> 10:10.610
There's no smoking in the building.

10:10.693 --> 10:13.195
At least give me a coffee, then.

10:17.283 --> 10:19.619
Ah, shit. It broke on me.

10:19.702 --> 10:22.455
That's gonna cost me later. Damn it.

10:22.538 --> 10:24.248
Ah, shit.

10:34.634 --> 10:37.511
By eight o'clock tonight,
Okinawa and the nearby area

10:37.595 --> 10:40.264
should see it, 120km over the western sea,

10:40.348 --> 10:42.600
and it's heading towards
the southern Jeju sea.

10:42.683 --> 10:46.187
Central pressure is 980,
wind velocity, 28, wind radius, 200.

11:01.077 --> 11:03.287
16 HOURS AGO

11:16.384 --> 11:17.593
Take it slow.

11:19.470 --> 11:20.513
Oh, Bo-mi.

11:21.138 --> 11:23.933
Appa. Did you sleep here?

11:24.684 --> 11:26.852
Yeah. Feel better? You okay now?

11:26.936 --> 11:29.146
Yeah, I'm okay. Everything's okay.

11:30.648 --> 11:32.441
The taxi is waiting for us. Let's go.

11:32.942 --> 11:34.985
Wait, you called a taxi?

11:35.069 --> 11:36.570
We can take my car.

11:37.947 --> 11:39.115
Come on, Bo-mi.

11:44.870 --> 11:45.830
Ah.

12:01.804 --> 12:04.974
Appa looked tired,
like he didn't sleep at all.

12:05.766 --> 12:08.561
Isn't it kinda rude
leaving him at the hospital like that?

12:08.644 --> 12:10.229
Since when did he

12:11.522 --> 12:13.941
start waiting for us like he cares at all?

12:14.024 --> 12:16.402
I've been waiting for over ten years.

12:16.485 --> 12:18.112
He can wait one night.

12:24.910 --> 12:26.662
You should rest until we get back.

12:46.515 --> 12:49.143
Let's go right now. Come and eat.

12:49.226 --> 12:50.352
Honey, breakfast.

12:50.436 --> 12:51.896
- Come on.
- It's mine!

12:51.979 --> 12:53.773
Goodness. Hey!

12:53.856 --> 12:56.609
Give it to me. No, let it go. Let it go.

12:56.692 --> 12:58.444
Come, sit down.
Both of you. Here we go.

12:58.527 --> 12:59.862
Oh, let's eat, boys.

12:59.945 --> 13:01.655
- Your backpack's packed?
- No.

13:01.739 --> 13:02.740
Go pack it right now.

13:02.823 --> 13:05.201
Hey, we'll do this later. Later.
Let's get you dressed.

13:05.284 --> 13:07.536
Stand up. Oh…

13:08.204 --> 13:09.705
Oh, my agenda.

13:10.289 --> 13:11.582
- Aah!
- Your agenda?

13:11.665 --> 13:14.043
- Do you know where it's gone to?
- No!

13:14.126 --> 13:15.252
Did you check the floor?

13:16.045 --> 13:17.463
One more.

13:17.546 --> 13:19.799
Oh, found it!

13:19.882 --> 13:23.427
I'll get you water. Put the agenda
in your backpack, okay?

13:23.511 --> 13:25.387
- Okay.
- Vroom, vroom!

13:25.471 --> 13:27.765
Vroom, vroom! Vroom!

13:29.850 --> 13:31.560
Honey, it's getting cold.

13:33.395 --> 13:34.355
Honey.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.151
He's working so hard.

13:40.152 --> 13:42.196
The Level Five exam isn't that hard.

13:44.865 --> 13:46.367
I'll just leave it.

13:47.284 --> 13:48.953
Come on! Boys!

13:57.920 --> 13:59.004
Hello, nice to meet you.

13:59.088 --> 14:01.131
I'm Forecaster Lee Si-woo
from Headquarters.

14:01.215 --> 14:02.216
How's it look now?

14:02.299 --> 14:04.552
When the trough gets higher
than five kilometers above ground,

14:04.635 --> 14:06.136
it should pull the typhoon.

14:06.220 --> 14:08.848
So the velocity of it will increase
between 20 and 25.

14:08.931 --> 14:10.057
Mm.

14:10.683 --> 14:13.435
If that's the rate,
it'll probably hit later than expected.

14:14.103 --> 14:16.480
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

14:17.189 --> 14:19.650
Oh, hi, I'm Forecaster Lee Si-woo
from Headquarters.

14:19.733 --> 14:21.735
- Your prediction?
- Sorry?

14:23.404 --> 14:24.405
Oh.

14:24.488 --> 14:27.825
Um, the way I see it,
the North Pacific anticyclone

14:27.908 --> 14:31.704
over by Japan is moving slower
than initially forecast.

14:31.787 --> 14:36.208
At this rate, I think it could slow down
to 10 or 15km per hour.

14:36.876 --> 14:37.835
Excuse me.

14:37.918 --> 14:40.963
Why do you think that would affect
the typhoon's course? Seems unlikely.

14:41.046 --> 14:44.717
I'm thinking of two specific cases
from 2002 and 2014,

14:44.800 --> 14:47.386
when the velocity
of the typhoon was slowed

14:47.469 --> 14:49.930
by the development
of that anticyclone in Japan.

14:51.223 --> 14:53.100
In 2014, it was Dolphin.

14:53.183 --> 14:55.477
- And in 2002…
- It was Haishen.

14:56.061 --> 15:00.482
Both cases had high variation
and turned into extratropical cyclones.

15:05.779 --> 15:06.947
And what was your name?

15:08.490 --> 15:10.826
Sorry, I'm sent
from the main Headquarters,

15:10.910 --> 15:12.494
Lee Si-woo, Severe Weather.

15:13.537 --> 15:16.165
I'm the Director. Sung Mi-jin here.

15:16.248 --> 15:17.625
Of course, nice to meet you.

15:17.708 --> 15:20.085
I should thank you for getting me here
earlier than expected.

15:21.587 --> 15:25.132
Each year, the climate totally transforms
beyond our predictions.

15:25.215 --> 15:28.344
Being here a week early
isn't enough to prepare sufficiently.

15:28.427 --> 15:29.678
What should I start with?

15:32.139 --> 15:34.308
Well, we've got a meeting in five minutes.

15:34.934 --> 15:36.143
Yes, ma'am.

15:51.367 --> 15:53.535
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:53.619 --> 15:54.870
Hello.

15:54.954 --> 15:56.789
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:56.872 --> 15:59.375
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

16:00.376 --> 16:02.044
Lee Si-woo's on the screen.

16:08.217 --> 16:09.760
Good morning, everyone.

16:09.843 --> 16:12.721
Good morning?
There's nothing good about it.

16:12.805 --> 16:14.098
A typhoon's on its way.

16:15.099 --> 16:17.101
Well,
that's an exciting morning, at least.

16:17.184 --> 16:18.477
I have great timing.

16:18.560 --> 16:20.521
I got to the typhoon center
on the right day.

16:20.604 --> 16:21.939
You're thrilled, I'm sure.

16:23.524 --> 16:27.194
My goodness, all that energy
is meant to be in the field.

16:29.697 --> 16:32.157
- All right. Typhoon's coming.
- Hello, sir.

16:32.241 --> 16:33.409
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

16:33.492 --> 16:34.451
Mm.

16:34.535 --> 16:35.995
General Director.

16:36.078 --> 16:38.414
You sent someone that actually knows
what they're doing.

16:38.497 --> 16:39.665
Oh, yeah?

16:40.416 --> 16:43.502
It wasn't up to me.
Thank Director Jin for him.

16:44.294 --> 16:45.671
Director Jin Ha-kyung?

16:45.754 --> 16:48.090
Well, it's nice to get
a good surprise for once.

16:51.051 --> 16:52.636
Let's get started.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.388
Satellite Center, what's your report?

16:54.471 --> 16:57.975
Two typhoons are developing
far out on the sea near Okinawa.

16:58.058 --> 17:01.353
One has a central pressure of 985

17:01.437 --> 17:04.732
and a maximum sustained wind
of 25m per second.

17:05.399 --> 17:07.026
Compared to three hours ago…

17:07.109 --> 17:08.444
I like you.

17:13.115 --> 17:15.743
I really like you a lot.

17:16.577 --> 17:19.121
Everything's so difficult.

17:26.628 --> 17:28.172
Why do you think it's difficult?

17:29.423 --> 17:31.592
We're different from each other.

17:33.010 --> 17:34.970
And I mostly like that.

17:36.680 --> 17:38.807
It's just difficult sometimes.

17:54.907 --> 17:57.451
At this phase, we'll see signs of it
starting tomorrow afternoon,

17:57.534 --> 17:58.744
is that correct?

17:58.827 --> 18:00.788
The moving velocity
has gone up.

18:00.871 --> 18:02.331
However, the surface temperature
in the sea out there

18:02.414 --> 18:04.291
is between 26 and 27 degrees.

18:04.374 --> 18:06.210
Quantity of the heat is less than ten.

18:06.293 --> 18:08.128
And the vertical shear
is under 10 degrees too.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.172
So I don't think we have
the right condition

18:10.255 --> 18:12.007
for the typhoon to continue developing.

18:13.675 --> 18:14.718
Typhoon Center.

18:14.802 --> 18:17.471
Any factors or theories
as to why the typhoon

18:17.554 --> 18:18.639
isn't gaining more energy?

18:19.598 --> 18:23.477
The warmest time of day is a few hours out
so the quantity of heat will rise.

18:24.061 --> 18:26.563
Especially looking at annual trend
showing the surface temperature

18:26.647 --> 18:28.190
is 3 degrees higher than last year.

18:28.273 --> 18:30.150
I would expect that the typhoon

18:30.234 --> 18:33.237
will continue gaining energy
even after entering our waters.

18:35.614 --> 18:38.408
What's its expected strength
when it travels inland?

18:38.492 --> 18:44.456
When it hits us,
the CI will be, uh, 2.5 to 3.0.

18:44.540 --> 18:48.418
The current trajectory makes it look
like Mokpo will be where it hits first.

18:48.502 --> 18:49.753
That's correct.

18:49.837 --> 18:54.049
If it does enter through Mokpo,
central pressure would be 970,

18:54.133 --> 18:58.220
and the maximum sustained wind
would be more than 30m per hour.

18:59.096 --> 19:01.265
With those measurements,
it would then be stronger

19:01.348 --> 19:03.684
than Prapiroon from 2018.

19:03.767 --> 19:06.937
AVERAGE DIFFERENCES
IN SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES

19:25.747 --> 19:27.916
The 14th of the season, Typhoon Ricky,

19:28.000 --> 19:30.002
is headed north toward
the Korean peninsula.

19:30.085 --> 19:32.796
On our chart here,
the typhoon's eye looks rather vivid,

19:32.880 --> 19:34.381
which means it will be quite powerful.

19:34.464 --> 19:39.136
In the center of the typhoon is a gale,
as strong as 100km per hour.

19:41.013 --> 19:43.140
If the forecast predicts a typhoon…

19:43.223 --> 19:44.516
- Eomma.
- Hm?

19:44.600 --> 19:47.060
Do you know how far we could go
at 100km an hour?

19:48.145 --> 19:49.354
I'm not…

19:49.938 --> 19:52.900
Seoul and Jeonju are about 200km away.

19:52.983 --> 19:56.069
So that means going a hundred,
we can get there in only two hours.

19:56.153 --> 19:57.362
Isn't the wind crazy?

19:57.446 --> 19:59.239
Wow. That's very interesting.

19:59.323 --> 20:01.617
I learned it on the trip to the KMA.

20:01.700 --> 20:04.161
Civilians are advised
to be on high alert. 

20:04.244 --> 20:06.455
Especially in areas with low visibility
or damage-prone.

20:06.538 --> 20:09.082
Those in farming areas
should avoid outdoor activities…

20:09.166 --> 20:12.002
It was pretty cool
going to see Dad at work.

20:12.085 --> 20:13.462
He's different in person.

20:16.465 --> 20:19.801
You ate the ham, why?
You know you're allergic to it.

20:19.885 --> 20:21.261
I guess I might have forgot.

20:22.179 --> 20:23.805
You can never forget about that.

20:24.389 --> 20:27.184
Don't you remember going to the hospital
when you were younger?

20:27.267 --> 20:29.019
'Cause you had rice
with pork sausage in it.

20:31.104 --> 20:32.105
Hmm.

20:32.648 --> 20:33.565
I'm hungry.

20:34.149 --> 20:35.692
Do we have any snacks?

20:40.405 --> 20:41.865
You won't be able to visit again.

20:42.449 --> 20:44.660
It's the busiest time
of the year for the KMA.

20:48.247 --> 20:51.083
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

20:52.417 --> 20:54.002
You should take your medication, too.

20:54.086 --> 20:55.796
It's right on the table if you look.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.675
- Eomma.
- Hm?

21:01.760 --> 21:03.595
You're getting divorced?

21:14.940 --> 21:16.525
Take your meds with your snack.

21:43.093 --> 21:44.344
How's your daughter doing?

21:45.178 --> 21:47.389
Oh, she's all right. She's back home.

21:49.391 --> 21:50.392
What a relief.

21:50.475 --> 21:52.394
It must have been stressful.

21:52.477 --> 21:55.230
It was. Her mom's taking care of her.

21:56.940 --> 22:00.027
I don't know what I've been doing
all this time.

22:01.153 --> 22:04.406
I thought it was good
to be such a hard worker, but…

22:05.449 --> 22:09.161
Looking back,
I was justifying being a lazy dad.

22:09.244 --> 22:13.165
Who doesn't know their kid's allergies?
I fed it to her.

22:14.416 --> 22:17.461
I put my own kid in the hospital.

22:22.174 --> 22:25.093
There are a million kinds
of dads out there.

22:25.969 --> 22:28.764
Having a dad
that's always available is great.

22:29.556 --> 22:32.392
There's a lot to be said for a dad
that works hard, though.

22:32.476 --> 22:33.769
I think it's equally great.

22:36.229 --> 22:37.397
Trying to make me feel better?

22:38.607 --> 22:39.983
If it's working.

22:40.067 --> 22:41.068
Yeah.

22:44.613 --> 22:45.489
I'm all right.

22:46.239 --> 22:49.034
Gosh. Two typhoons are coming in
any day now.

22:49.117 --> 22:50.369
I need my head in the game.

22:50.952 --> 22:54.164
I know. And one could be stronger
than Prapiroon, lucky us.

22:54.247 --> 22:57.959
Also, I wanted to say,
I think you made a great call earlier.

22:58.835 --> 23:00.962
Sending Lee Si-woo out in the field.

23:02.756 --> 23:04.674
Thank you. It worked out, huh?

23:11.473 --> 23:13.475
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

23:13.558 --> 23:15.185
Thank you. Thank you.

23:20.065 --> 23:22.609
How many died from Typhoon Prapiroon?

23:22.692 --> 23:26.571
Thirty-eight deaths and missing.
Three hundred sixty-six injured.

23:26.655 --> 23:29.074
Oh. Was property damage that bad, too?

23:29.157 --> 23:32.619
Seventy billion for the capital.
Casualties are more important, though.

23:33.286 --> 23:35.789
Also, is something going on
with Miss Chae?

23:37.874 --> 23:39.543
I just haven't seen her in a while.

23:40.127 --> 23:43.213
Oh, she needed some time off.
I told her so.

23:44.339 --> 23:46.299
Are you…

23:48.093 --> 23:49.136
Are we what?

23:49.803 --> 23:51.721
…gonna have a baby?

23:56.309 --> 23:58.145
- Assistant Director Kim.
- Yes?

23:58.228 --> 24:01.064
Don't you have to tell the press
the briefing time?

24:01.148 --> 24:03.859
Oh, right. I'm so out of it.

24:31.136 --> 24:32.179
Dong-jin.

24:32.262 --> 24:33.346
Yu-jin!

24:34.306 --> 24:36.766
- Come here!
- I'm here!

24:36.850 --> 24:39.227
How have you been, big guy?

24:39.311 --> 24:40.854
What took you so long?

24:41.438 --> 24:44.107
- I missed you with my whole heart.
- Did you?

24:44.816 --> 24:47.319
- Oh, boy. You're growing, aren't you?
- Huh?

24:48.111 --> 24:50.947
- Here you are. Hey, welcome.
- Hey.

24:52.199 --> 24:53.366
Is his dad here?

24:53.450 --> 24:55.368
Oh, he's moving the boat
before the typhoon.

24:55.452 --> 24:56.912
- Come in.
- Mm.

24:58.246 --> 24:59.331
Let's go.

25:05.378 --> 25:09.174
JEJU OFFICE

25:11.218 --> 25:13.720
Check the AWS.
Make sure it's working before you go.

25:13.803 --> 25:14.721
Sure, I will.

25:15.972 --> 25:18.642
- You're tagging along?
- Since I'm gonna be here a while,

25:18.725 --> 25:20.977
I thought I should know
where they're stationed, don't you?

25:21.061 --> 25:23.980
Ah, you're a real weather guy, huh?
Don't work too late.

25:24.064 --> 25:25.941
- Yeah, thanks.
- Okay. Let's go.

25:33.823 --> 25:35.158
What's going on?

25:35.242 --> 25:36.868
Why is it slowed down like that?

25:36.952 --> 25:40.038
They're figuring it out,
we're not sure why at this point in time.

25:40.872 --> 25:43.625
Been over the sea southwest of Jeju
for an hour now.

25:44.668 --> 25:46.711
What now, huh?

25:47.462 --> 25:50.799
The typhoon has stopped moving,
stuck over the Jeju sea.

25:50.882 --> 25:53.677
We're looking into the cause as we speak.

25:53.760 --> 25:55.595
Oh, no…

25:59.432 --> 26:02.394
It's currently 7 p.m.,
and Typhoon Ricky has suddenly turned

26:02.477 --> 26:03.687
towards the east.

26:03.770 --> 26:06.273
It's stagnant to the southwest.
I need an explanation.

26:06.982 --> 26:09.401
The upper and lower parts
could have separated

26:09.484 --> 26:11.444
and influenced its movement, right?

26:11.528 --> 26:12.779
It is a possibility.

26:12.862 --> 26:15.574
It's difficult to determine
with only satellite pictures.

26:18.034 --> 26:21.079
I'd like to see
the current adiabatic chart in Jeju.

26:21.162 --> 26:22.872
Could your team do that?

26:22.956 --> 26:26.501
We have to do
a sonde observation from Seongsan.

26:26.585 --> 26:28.712
The observation vehicle
is in Seongsan now.

26:28.795 --> 26:32.841
Well, my team happens to have
our observation van in Seongsan currently.

26:33.425 --> 26:35.635
What do you think?
Should we do the sonde or not?

26:38.847 --> 26:41.182
You sure the adiabatic chart
will be enough for you?

26:41.766 --> 26:43.226
Yes. We just need to check

26:43.310 --> 26:45.729
the upper and lower parts
from about five kilometers above.

26:51.151 --> 26:54.029
SPECIAL OBSERVATION VEHICLE

27:12.380 --> 27:13.506
Excuse me.

27:13.590 --> 27:16.676
How many AWSs are on Jeju Island in total?

27:16.760 --> 27:18.011
Twenty-five altogether.

27:18.094 --> 27:19.262
Oh.

27:20.013 --> 27:21.765
Will we check all those today?

27:21.848 --> 27:24.351
Hey, the island is huge.
We'd never make it back.

27:24.434 --> 27:27.312
We're on a time crunch, so we're
only checking eight on the eastern side.

27:27.395 --> 27:28.813
Okay.

27:33.068 --> 27:34.361
Let's go.

27:35.028 --> 27:36.571
Huh? Si-woo, oppa?

27:38.865 --> 27:40.408
Oh, what brings you to Jeju?

27:40.492 --> 27:43.662
Uh, I'm visiting my mom
and step-family.

27:44.329 --> 27:45.163
Oh.

27:45.246 --> 27:47.582
This is my mom and my brother.

27:47.666 --> 27:49.292
Oh, hello.

27:50.126 --> 27:52.045
- Hi.
- What brings you out here?

27:52.128 --> 27:54.255
Oh, the typhoon center is out here.

27:54.339 --> 27:55.423
Oh, hey.

27:55.507 --> 27:57.509
- You work at the KMA, don't you?
- Mm-hm.

27:58.093 --> 27:59.260
I do, and it's great.

27:59.844 --> 28:02.138
Are you my sister's boyfriend?

28:02.222 --> 28:03.723
- Uh…
- Goodness.

28:03.807 --> 28:05.850
What are you talking about? She's married.

28:05.934 --> 28:08.395
You've met your brother-in-law.

28:08.478 --> 28:09.979
Oh, yeah, that guy.

28:12.524 --> 28:15.110
Mr. Lee,
Director Sung just called.

28:15.193 --> 28:17.696
They want a sonde observation
in Seongsan right now.

28:17.779 --> 28:18.988
Oh, uh, right now?

28:19.072 --> 28:22.075
Yeah. It sounds like the typhoon
isn't doing what we thought it was.

28:22.158 --> 28:23.952
- Oh--
- Oh, can I come, too?

28:24.452 --> 28:25.995
Oh, no, Dong-jin.

28:28.248 --> 28:30.750
Please? Can I go with you?

28:30.834 --> 28:32.836
Yu-jin, can I go with him?

28:32.919 --> 28:34.629
Calm down. They've got work to do.

28:34.713 --> 28:37.882
It'd be so cool, please? Please.

28:37.966 --> 28:39.217
I'll be good.

28:39.300 --> 28:41.511
Uh, would it be all right
if they tag along?

28:41.594 --> 28:43.138
They could watch from the car.

28:48.935 --> 28:51.396
Can they go?

29:01.448 --> 29:04.409
- What do you want?
- There's a typhoon coming in.

29:04.492 --> 29:06.411
Took you long enough to call.

29:06.494 --> 29:08.163
On the news, they kept saying that

29:08.246 --> 29:11.416
a typhoon's coming
and we better prepare for a big one.

29:13.084 --> 29:14.961
Okay, then. That was all.

29:15.044 --> 29:18.339
Hey, hey. You're just
hanging up without asking about me?

29:18.423 --> 29:20.091
Why? Do you have something to say?

29:22.927 --> 29:24.262
That man that works for you.

29:24.846 --> 29:26.556
If it's about Assistant Shin,
I'm hanging up.

29:26.639 --> 29:29.601
Oh, no. Oh, no. I don't mean that one.

29:29.684 --> 29:32.645
You know, the one that looks young
that I met in the elevator,

29:32.729 --> 29:34.147
the guy that's staying with you.

29:34.230 --> 29:35.774
Was his name Lee Si-woo? Uh…

29:36.566 --> 29:37.692
What about him?

29:39.152 --> 29:40.445
Did he say anything?

29:41.029 --> 29:42.489
Lee Si-woo? Why would he?

29:42.572 --> 29:45.158
Did-- Some-- What are you talking about?

29:45.241 --> 29:47.619
I got dinner with him. Why?

29:47.702 --> 29:50.497
Eomma, you got dinner with him?
When was that--

29:50.580 --> 29:51.790
I mean… Why?

29:51.873 --> 29:53.708
That's inappropriate and it's weird.

29:53.792 --> 29:56.419
What was I supposed to do,
you wouldn't answer your phone,

29:56.503 --> 29:58.546
and I had to know about the guy above you.

29:58.630 --> 30:01.591
Eomma, did you talk to Si-woo
about Assistant Shin and me?

30:01.674 --> 30:04.636
Shame on you. Shame on you
for not picking up my call.

30:04.719 --> 30:06.888
You should've learned by now, huh?

30:07.472 --> 30:09.349
I had to do something.
You wouldn't answer.

30:09.933 --> 30:12.435
Well, it… it's still really wrong!

30:12.519 --> 30:15.230
How is it wrong? What's wrong about it?

30:15.313 --> 30:17.190
His director's mother treated him
to a dinner.

30:17.273 --> 30:19.192
Why are you acting like it's illegal?

30:23.446 --> 30:25.532
It's not how it was a long time ago, Mom.

30:25.615 --> 30:28.535
It's bad enough you met
my subordinate in private,

30:28.618 --> 30:30.453
but you asked questions about me, too?

30:31.204 --> 30:33.790
If you do it again,
and I'll never see you again, ever.

30:33.873 --> 30:37.252
Ugh. No, you're so dramatic. Calm down.

30:38.628 --> 30:39.629
Hey.

30:41.047 --> 30:44.092
Have you noticed how he is?

30:44.175 --> 30:45.343
What?

30:45.927 --> 30:48.596
I-- I think the Lee guy
has feelings for you.

30:52.976 --> 30:55.103
The way he talks about you,
I think he has…

30:55.186 --> 30:57.522
What's the word for it?
Uh, it's something like…

30:57.605 --> 30:58.982
Um, wait, a mush.

30:59.065 --> 31:02.318
No, a crush. He has a crush on you.

31:04.195 --> 31:07.198
You still there? Hey, did you…

31:07.282 --> 31:08.908
Hey, Ha-kyung, did you…

31:10.702 --> 31:12.412
She won't let it go.

31:16.124 --> 31:17.709
MOM

31:22.964 --> 31:24.340
Well, that was odd.

31:24.841 --> 31:27.594
Maybe she likes him, too?

31:28.595 --> 31:31.306
Eh, there's no way.

31:31.890 --> 31:34.851
Tae-kyung would, but Ha-kyung would never.

31:34.934 --> 31:37.270
He's way too high risk,
she always wants someone that's safe.

31:49.991 --> 31:51.409
Doors opening.

32:00.668 --> 32:01.836
Doors closing.

32:04.422 --> 32:06.674
- Leaving?
- Mm-hm.

32:07.926 --> 32:10.720
- You're not, though?
- Mm-mm, just getting dinner.

32:11.220 --> 32:12.347
Mm.

32:19.687 --> 32:20.980
Could I eat with you?

32:40.792 --> 32:43.711
- The wind's picking up.
- Yeah, it is.

32:45.046 --> 32:47.006
DATE OF DATA
JULY 30, 2022

32:48.466 --> 32:49.634
I got it.

32:55.848 --> 32:57.642
You have to let it go and call.

32:58.267 --> 33:01.479
- What are you saying?
- You want Ki-jun to call first, don't you?

33:01.562 --> 33:02.855
How did you know?

33:02.939 --> 33:05.525
It's obvious. A mother knows these things.

33:07.860 --> 33:11.280
Don't drag this out,
not when you're married.

33:12.031 --> 33:16.577
It's best if you call today,
say you'll let it go, and go back.

33:17.203 --> 33:19.664
Eomma. I just got here.

33:19.747 --> 33:22.458
You can visit any time.
Come on the holidays.

33:24.335 --> 33:25.670
Why?

33:25.753 --> 33:29.340
You're worried that I'll mess up
my first marriage like you did?

33:31.676 --> 33:32.802
Mm-hm.

33:34.053 --> 33:35.096
That's right.

33:36.389 --> 33:40.143
I got married when I was too young,
I really didn't know.

33:41.144 --> 33:43.813
The pettiness only made things worse.

33:44.397 --> 33:46.482
Okay, let's move on.

33:49.360 --> 33:52.572
I know Ki-jun is a good man.
See, mothers know.

33:53.990 --> 33:57.618
I don't know what you're fighting about,
you have to let it go, hm?

33:58.870 --> 34:01.164
Oh, baby, you know that.

34:02.373 --> 34:05.168
I can take care of it. Thanks.

34:05.918 --> 34:06.836
Drop it.

34:15.511 --> 34:16.387
You want a drink?

34:17.221 --> 34:19.265
I have to go back after this.

34:19.348 --> 34:20.975
Two typhoons are coming in soon.

34:33.071 --> 34:35.198
Was I so frustrating
you couldn't stand it, Ha-kyung?

34:37.950 --> 34:41.662
Am I just an untrustworthy idiot
and a total loser?

34:44.749 --> 34:46.167
I could ask the same to you.

34:47.627 --> 34:51.297
Was I so work-obsessed, insensitive,
that I made you fall out of love?

34:52.799 --> 34:53.925
I mean…

34:54.008 --> 34:56.385
I can't really say you weren't.

34:56.469 --> 34:58.387
Honestly, with some distance, though,

34:58.471 --> 35:00.556
you're great
and anyone's lucky to have you.

35:01.516 --> 35:02.850
You're smart,

35:02.934 --> 35:05.311
and responsible,
and you're really good at keeping calm.

35:06.104 --> 35:11.734
And also, if I wasn't competing with work,
you were really compassionate and kind.

35:11.818 --> 35:16.280
I think we just weren't the right match
for each other.

35:17.698 --> 35:18.825
You're okay.

35:19.492 --> 35:21.953
You go all-in at work,
even with things you've never done.

35:22.036 --> 35:24.080
You have courage and it shows.

35:25.039 --> 35:28.501
I will say you did some things
that were tough to work through.

35:29.919 --> 35:31.170
But you're not awful.

35:33.965 --> 35:36.634
You're not the right one for me.

35:41.180 --> 35:44.100
I didn't know you saw me in that way.

35:45.268 --> 35:46.477
And honestly,

35:46.561 --> 35:50.606
I thought you looked down on me
the whole relationship.

35:50.690 --> 35:52.859
"Oh God, what an idiot."

35:52.942 --> 35:55.361
"How did he make it this far?"
That sort of thing.

35:56.904 --> 35:58.865
I wanted your best at what you do.

35:58.948 --> 36:00.575
I know you're good at your work.

36:05.663 --> 36:07.874
We should've said all this sooner, huh?

36:10.918 --> 36:13.671
Maybe we didn't realize
we had to say it out loud.

36:14.297 --> 36:15.840
But I wouldn't have known.

36:16.674 --> 36:17.967
I misunderstood you

36:18.968 --> 36:20.178
and got resentful.

36:20.761 --> 36:21.846
You did.

36:22.471 --> 36:26.517
There are so many things we wouldn't know
unless we express ourselves.

36:29.770 --> 36:30.813
It's true.

36:30.897 --> 36:33.774
There are so many things we wouldn't know
unless we share them.

36:36.194 --> 36:41.073
So why did we expect each other
to know these without saying anything?

36:48.456 --> 36:50.082
Oh? That's rain.

36:50.166 --> 36:51.959
Mr. Lee, I'll be right back.

36:52.043 --> 36:53.002
Okay.

37:47.598 --> 37:48.599
Where are you?

37:48.683 --> 37:50.726
At least tell me where you're staying.

38:40.443 --> 38:41.610
Si-woo…

38:45.990 --> 38:46.907
Si-woo, oppa!

38:49.452 --> 38:50.536
Si-woo!

38:51.454 --> 38:53.622
- Si-woo, can you hear me?
- Mr. Lee!

38:53.706 --> 38:55.291
Don't move too much.

38:57.668 --> 38:58.919
Stay with us, Mr. Lee.

39:04.800 --> 39:06.969
We can't just ignore it.

39:07.053 --> 39:10.264
PRESENT

39:11.140 --> 39:13.225
Can you check in with the hospital again?

39:13.309 --> 39:14.268
Huh?

39:14.352 --> 39:16.395
If there's news about Lee Si-woo,

39:16.479 --> 39:18.439
- I'd like to know.
- Oh, okay.

39:25.863 --> 39:28.699
Going on with the last update
we heard from Jeju,

39:28.783 --> 39:31.535
he, thankfully,
isn't in critical condition currently.

39:32.995 --> 39:34.038
So you…

39:35.498 --> 39:37.500
- Huh?
- You're saying…

39:38.084 --> 39:40.461
you're not gonna compensate him
for his injury,

39:40.544 --> 39:43.631
because it's not critical enough,
is that it?

39:44.340 --> 39:45.716
No, sir.

39:46.258 --> 39:48.969
We'll make sure he's taken care of,
financially and otherwise.

39:49.595 --> 39:51.597
I said that only
because I thought you want to know

39:51.680 --> 39:54.975
- how your son's doing in the hospital.
- You're trying to avoid things.

39:55.893 --> 39:57.728
This isn't my first rodeo.

39:57.812 --> 40:02.441
I know you're doing damage control,
'cause you cheapskates are all the same.

40:02.525 --> 40:03.651
You don't wanna pay out!

40:03.734 --> 40:05.403
It's not gonna work on us!

40:05.903 --> 40:09.198
I think, Mr. Lee,
that you're way out of line.

40:09.281 --> 40:10.366
I don't want to hear it!

40:11.450 --> 40:13.994
So we should cut to the chase,

40:14.078 --> 40:16.622
and decide the amount,
then we'll go our separate ways!

40:17.498 --> 40:18.707
Okay, listen.

40:21.460 --> 40:22.503
Yeah?

40:24.171 --> 40:25.005
What is it?

40:25.089 --> 40:28.008
I got off the phone
with the hospital just now.

40:28.092 --> 40:30.010
They transferred him to the general ward.

40:30.094 --> 40:32.304
- His eyes were slightly injured.
- He…

40:33.139 --> 40:34.932
hurt his eyes?

40:36.308 --> 40:37.435
- Oh.
- Well, then…

40:39.854 --> 40:43.190
That bad of an injury counts
for disability level one, yeah?

40:43.941 --> 40:45.609
He could still fully recover.

40:45.693 --> 40:47.319
It's not a guaranteed disability,
you know?

40:47.403 --> 40:49.405
I know what it's like to be a dad
worried about his kid,

40:49.488 --> 40:51.657
- but you're going overboard.
- You're gonna judge me?

40:51.740 --> 40:53.742
What you guys are saying is too much!

40:54.410 --> 40:55.995
You're responsible! Without you, idiots,

40:56.078 --> 40:57.705
he wouldn't be laying in a hospital bed.

40:57.788 --> 41:00.749
So, I'm here for accountability,
'cause you hurt my boy!

41:00.833 --> 41:02.751
You're gonna fix his eyes?

41:04.336 --> 41:06.130
You're right. I'm sorry, Mr. Lee.

41:06.213 --> 41:07.214
That's right.

41:07.840 --> 41:10.009
Director Lady understands.

41:10.092 --> 41:12.970
So how about we go to Jeju together?

41:14.722 --> 41:15.764
What?

41:16.348 --> 41:19.518
You're so worried about how he is,
we should go and see for ourselves.

41:19.602 --> 41:21.770
Then we'll know
how this discussion should go.

41:28.903 --> 41:29.737
Director Jin.

41:29.820 --> 41:32.781
I heard what you said about him earlier.
He's your only son.

41:33.574 --> 41:34.533
Yeah.

41:35.409 --> 41:38.704
I've gotta take care of him
with this compensation.

41:38.787 --> 41:41.165
- Just for his sake, we gotta figure this--
- That's step two.

41:41.248 --> 41:44.126
First, you should go
and see how he is, if he's okay.

41:45.503 --> 41:48.839
We can't determine any compensation
until we've assessed things ourselves.

41:52.384 --> 41:54.553
We'll take the first flight out tomorrow.

41:54.637 --> 41:56.138
Is that all right, sir?

41:56.222 --> 41:59.058
Yeah. Of course. Get your tickets.

41:59.141 --> 42:00.726
You can handle it on your own?

42:01.352 --> 42:02.478
Yes, I can.

42:03.521 --> 42:05.105
See you at the airport early tomorrow.

42:18.911 --> 42:19.954
Huh?

42:21.121 --> 42:22.915
Why do you need to tag along?

42:22.998 --> 42:26.460
If they need extra help,
they should get someone from HR.

42:26.544 --> 42:28.504
I have some urgent business out there.

42:29.088 --> 42:30.047
I can't.

42:30.130 --> 42:32.633
There are two major typhoons
coming any day now.

42:33.259 --> 42:34.843
You won't let me go?

42:35.636 --> 42:37.596
Mm-mm. No way.

42:39.056 --> 42:42.017
Then I have to take a leave of absence.

42:42.685 --> 42:44.520
- You what?
- The typhoons?

42:45.229 --> 42:48.023
Yeah, it's important,
and we have to keep everyone safe.

42:48.107 --> 42:51.527
But, you know, I've never taken
a day off in typhoon season.

42:51.610 --> 42:53.404
Not since I began here.

42:53.487 --> 42:55.114
Even when I needed to.

42:55.614 --> 42:57.032
Not a half-day, not a long lunch.

42:57.116 --> 42:59.243
Every year, I give everything to this job.

42:59.326 --> 43:00.661
Yeah, and your co-workers do, too.

43:00.744 --> 43:01.829
That's my point.

43:01.912 --> 43:04.248
Everyone here works like I do,
then they'll be able

43:04.331 --> 43:05.791
to cover me for a day.

43:06.584 --> 43:09.086
I'll ask you again,
can I take the time off?

43:09.169 --> 43:11.463
Oh, why can't you do this another season?

43:11.547 --> 43:12.673
I wish I could.

43:13.632 --> 43:15.759
Except Yu-jin left me now, so I…

43:18.345 --> 43:19.179
Huh?

43:19.763 --> 43:21.140
Is that why?

43:21.223 --> 43:23.601
That's why she hasn't been attending
any of the briefings?

43:26.395 --> 43:30.190
Our whole life together
could fall apart in pieces.

43:32.234 --> 43:33.569
Can you let me go?

43:44.913 --> 43:46.081
Director Jin.

43:46.915 --> 43:50.419
Is there a way you could take me
to Jeju Island?

43:53.255 --> 43:54.381
Oh.

44:50.688 --> 44:51.814
Hm?

44:53.816 --> 44:55.109
Another all-nighter?

44:55.192 --> 44:56.610
Yeah.

44:56.694 --> 44:58.904
Why… Why are you here so early?

44:59.488 --> 45:01.115
I needed to talk with you.

45:09.957 --> 45:12.000
Tae-kyung, breakfast is ready.

45:13.752 --> 45:15.087
That girl.

45:15.170 --> 45:17.297
Tae-kyung, come out and eat.

45:22.720 --> 45:23.762
Hm?

45:24.263 --> 45:26.140
She's never out this early.

45:36.275 --> 45:37.484
Ah.

45:50.539 --> 45:52.875
You must be tired from working all night.

45:52.958 --> 45:55.085
You could have called
and rescheduled for later.

45:55.961 --> 45:58.172
Aren't you supposed
to sign this contract by noon?

45:58.255 --> 46:01.383
Yeah, but it's not really
a huge deal at all.

46:01.467 --> 46:03.343
So…

46:04.636 --> 46:07.639
I looked over the contract a few times

46:07.723 --> 46:09.975
- and something stood out.
- Hm?

46:11.518 --> 46:14.396
Right here, the "exclusive publication."

46:14.480 --> 46:15.939
What does this mean, exactly?

46:17.274 --> 46:19.109
Oh, I don't really know.

46:20.611 --> 46:24.323
What about all these restrictions
on royalties?

46:24.406 --> 46:28.911
Uh, that's just saying how much I get
when each book gets sold in stores.

46:29.953 --> 46:33.665
Then shouldn't Article 11 leave you
with franchise rights?

46:37.586 --> 46:40.380
Why, should I ask for that?

46:42.966 --> 46:44.092
Yeah, uh…

46:44.760 --> 46:47.095
Can I talk to whoever sent you this thing?

46:47.179 --> 46:48.514
What?

46:56.855 --> 46:59.149
Hello, it's Jin Tae-kyung.
Someone wants to talk…

46:59.233 --> 47:01.819
Oh, here he is. Here.

47:01.902 --> 47:02.861
Thanks.

47:04.530 --> 47:05.614
Yes, hello?

47:05.697 --> 47:09.576
Well, I have some questions
about the contract.

47:09.660 --> 47:12.120
Starting with Article 11, that won't do.

47:12.871 --> 47:16.959
Also, we need a fair percentage
on royalties, understand me?

47:17.876 --> 47:19.920
She's the illustrator
and the author of everything.

47:20.003 --> 47:21.672
You just print it for her.

47:21.755 --> 47:22.673
Who am I?

47:25.008 --> 47:26.802
Well, I'm her manager, obviously.

47:28.929 --> 47:29.972
Yes.

47:31.473 --> 47:32.850
That's all right, and please,

47:32.933 --> 47:34.977
give us a call back
when it's been worked out.

47:35.060 --> 47:35.936
Great.

47:38.105 --> 47:41.733
They're gonna adjust the percentage
for your royalties.

47:41.817 --> 47:43.360
They'll get back to you soon.

47:43.443 --> 47:44.903
I see.

47:44.987 --> 47:47.781
You have to ask them questions.

47:47.865 --> 47:50.367
Make sure you understand
and have a fair deal,

47:50.450 --> 47:52.286
or they'll pull a fast one on you.

47:53.161 --> 47:55.664
You could lose your rights
to your characters and more

47:55.747 --> 47:57.416
on top of them for the royalties.

47:57.499 --> 48:00.335
You have to be careful
with anything they give you, okay?

48:00.419 --> 48:01.962
I've been divorced before.

48:04.423 --> 48:05.299
And?

48:06.550 --> 48:08.969
What? Oh.

48:09.052 --> 48:10.929
I thought you should know.

48:15.893 --> 48:19.897
There's a myth about penguins
that everyone thinks it's true.

48:19.980 --> 48:21.106
What is it?

48:21.189 --> 48:22.858
That they mate for life.

48:23.775 --> 48:24.776
That's not true?

48:25.569 --> 48:28.614
There was a documentary
where this penguin couple

48:28.697 --> 48:30.908
worked together to raise their chick.

48:30.991 --> 48:32.492
That was breeding season.

48:33.076 --> 48:35.495
The next year, if it wasn't a good match,

48:35.579 --> 48:37.331
they're free to find
a new partner to be with.

48:38.749 --> 48:39.708
But why…

48:40.542 --> 48:43.712
are you telling me about this now?

48:45.297 --> 48:48.091
'Cause animals don't care
if anyone's had a mate before.

48:54.848 --> 48:56.892
Would you eat breakfast with me?

48:57.476 --> 48:58.352
Yeah.

49:10.572 --> 49:12.950
Well, I'll listen. But you should eat.

49:21.500 --> 49:22.709
What is this?

49:26.630 --> 49:28.048
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

49:28.131 --> 49:29.758
Look it over and sign it.

49:36.974 --> 49:39.685
- Sweetheart, this--
- Don't think this was a sudden decision.

49:40.268 --> 49:41.478
It was a long time coming.

49:41.561 --> 49:44.189
I hope you respect that this is my choice.

49:54.950 --> 49:57.786
I'm so sorry, Hyang-rae.

49:58.495 --> 50:01.873
I made you raise Bo-mi
all on your own and…

50:02.374 --> 50:05.794
You must have felt so alone
while I was gone.

50:05.877 --> 50:07.462
And truly, I apologize.

50:09.798 --> 50:11.008
It's just…

50:13.218 --> 50:14.761
I never would've chosen to leave you.

50:14.845 --> 50:17.681
- It was always for work.
- No more excuses.

50:18.265 --> 50:22.019
And at first, you had no say,
it had to be either Busan or Namhae.

50:22.102 --> 50:24.938
Neither one was home for us.
Either way, you'd be leaving.

50:25.022 --> 50:27.858
But over time,
I realized you like being gone.

50:30.610 --> 50:31.570
Hmm.

50:31.653 --> 50:34.406
You're right. I did.

50:35.532 --> 50:38.285
- And she got to you.
- Who got to who?

50:38.368 --> 50:40.912
The TV woman that speaks for the KMA.

50:40.996 --> 50:43.540
- Jin Ha-kyung.
- Director Jin? What?

50:43.623 --> 50:45.459
What? What?

50:45.542 --> 50:46.918
I saw it.

50:47.627 --> 50:49.671
You were leaving the KMA together.

51:03.060 --> 51:05.270
What? No! It's not…

51:05.771 --> 51:08.398
You're totally misunderstanding.
It wasn't that.

51:12.027 --> 51:13.236
It was work.

51:14.196 --> 51:15.614
Ask anyone.

51:15.697 --> 51:17.449
And it wasn't just me staying there.

51:17.532 --> 51:20.118
There was another forecaster,
Si-woo there, too.

51:20.202 --> 51:22.704
She was being nice
by letting us stay there

51:22.788 --> 51:23.789
instead of at the office.

51:25.457 --> 51:27.000
It's really not what you think.

51:27.084 --> 51:29.544
A-- Ask Si-woo.
He'll tell you exactly the same thing.

51:29.628 --> 51:32.172
And I swear on Bo-mi.
I swear it's really true.

51:32.756 --> 51:34.966
You're not really bringing Bo-mi
into this, are you?

51:35.884 --> 51:37.302
Right, I'm not.

51:38.053 --> 51:40.013
But I… I'd never do that.

51:40.097 --> 51:42.682
You know me,
it's insane that you'd think that at all.

51:45.811 --> 51:48.063
It is. And that's what I thought, too.

51:49.147 --> 51:51.149
In all that time,
it never crossed my mind.

51:51.233 --> 51:53.276
"Maybe he's cheating,
or has another family."

51:53.360 --> 51:55.028
Because I trusted you.

51:55.779 --> 51:57.656
So when I finally caught you…

51:58.949 --> 52:00.700
it hurt beyond words.

52:01.451 --> 52:03.537
Okay, Hyang-rae. I…

52:05.664 --> 52:08.375
How long did you actually stay with us
after you transferred?

52:09.000 --> 52:12.712
It seemed best for everyone,
you and Bo-mi, if I left and stayed away.

52:15.090 --> 52:17.050
No excuses, Dong-han.

52:17.134 --> 52:20.137
You chose to run away because
you couldn't face that we're hurting.

52:20.220 --> 52:21.471
Don't blame us for that.

52:22.681 --> 52:25.142
Do you have any idea
how much it hurt us that you left again?

52:28.436 --> 52:32.232
It was childish of me.

52:39.322 --> 52:41.366
Why do you make me feel so miserable?

52:43.493 --> 52:45.495
What did I do
to make you hate me like this?

52:50.876 --> 52:52.419
I apologize.

52:53.128 --> 52:54.254
Hyang-rae.

52:54.754 --> 52:56.298
I'll come home and make it right.

52:56.381 --> 52:58.341
You think that's still an option?

52:58.425 --> 53:00.218
Please, one more chance.

53:00.302 --> 53:02.304
No, no more. Enough.

53:03.096 --> 53:05.015
Just be a decent man for once and sign it.

53:05.098 --> 53:05.974
Sign the paper

53:06.057 --> 53:08.727
and we can both go
and move on with our lives.

53:09.436 --> 53:11.730
It's what's best for everyone, hm?

54:19.881 --> 54:21.925
What's the patient's
full name?

54:22.008 --> 54:22.842
Lee Si-woo.

54:22.926 --> 54:25.512
And who is Lee Si-woo to each of you?

54:25.595 --> 54:29.849
Uh, I'm his dad. Lee Si-woo's my son.

54:29.933 --> 54:32.018
My only kid. I'm his guardian.

54:33.186 --> 54:35.772
Over there to the right. He's Room 305.

54:35.855 --> 54:37.023
Thank you, miss.

54:37.107 --> 54:38.316
Also…

55:32.287 --> 55:33.455
Are you okay?

55:59.022 --> 56:00.231
I'm better now.

56:07.405 --> 56:08.406
No tears.

56:26.257 --> 56:27.592
Hey, Si-woo.

56:29.010 --> 56:31.346
What's wrong with you, huh?

56:31.930 --> 56:33.515
What's on your face?

56:33.598 --> 56:35.517
Tell me everything. What did they do?

56:36.810 --> 56:37.936
Dad, is that you?

56:38.019 --> 56:39.979
Yes. It's me. I'm here. I'll fix it.

56:40.063 --> 56:42.023
Oh, God. Look at you.

56:42.107 --> 56:45.402
He's way worse than I thought he was.

56:47.070 --> 56:49.447
How did you get here? Uh, no.

56:49.531 --> 56:51.324
- Why are you here?
- Come on, kid.

56:51.408 --> 56:53.993
What dad wouldn't come
when his only son gets hurt?

56:54.077 --> 56:57.205
I've been calling and calling you.
You wouldn't pick up, though.

56:57.288 --> 57:00.041
I was going crazy,
so I hit up the guys at your work.

57:00.125 --> 57:03.253
- You went to Headquarters?
- Hey, don't you worry, though.

57:03.336 --> 57:05.755
I went in and talked
to the head director guy.

57:05.839 --> 57:09.384
He knows he better get you
what he owes you, or else, believe me…

57:09.467 --> 57:11.845
I got it all under control, okay, kid?

57:12.512 --> 57:17.767
Oh, and it's just your eyes?
Did they check the rest of you, huh?

57:17.851 --> 57:20.311
I'll do it. Let me look.

57:20.812 --> 57:24.190
Hey, you got to tell me
where else you're hurt.

57:24.274 --> 57:26.818
We've got to milk 'em
for everything that we can.

57:26.901 --> 57:27.902
Got it?

57:29.737 --> 57:32.282
- Director Jin.
- Huh?

57:32.365 --> 57:33.741
Get this man out, please.

57:34.659 --> 57:35.785
Huh?

57:37.704 --> 57:39.372
- Si-woo.
- I want you out.

57:39.456 --> 57:42.041
You should leave.
Seoul is missing you, I'm sure.

57:43.251 --> 57:45.378
Are you kidding?

57:45.462 --> 57:48.214
I'm gonna be at your side
every second, don't worry.

57:48.298 --> 57:50.216
I want you to leave me alone!

57:54.471 --> 57:57.098
You don't know what you're saying.
How's your head?

57:57.182 --> 58:00.268
- How's your legs?
- Hi. I heard the guardian was present.

58:00.351 --> 58:03.646
Yeah, yeah, yeah, that's me.
Lee Si-woo means everything to me.

58:03.730 --> 58:06.733
Yes, good to meet you.
May I please have a word with you outside?

58:06.816 --> 58:08.234
Uh-huh. Yeah.

58:10.487 --> 58:12.197
- Let's go.
- Okay.

58:21.414 --> 58:22.373
He's just…

58:24.000 --> 58:26.586
acting out,
'cause he's so worried about you.

58:27.754 --> 58:29.422
He's not capable of that.

58:30.548 --> 58:32.050
He doesn't care that I'm injured.

58:32.675 --> 58:36.179
There's only one thing he came for,
and it has nothing to do with his son.

58:36.763 --> 58:39.224
- Si-woo--
- That's just the kind of bad father he is!

58:40.767 --> 58:43.561
You should not have brought him here!
Do you get it now?

59:03.414 --> 59:06.042
Oh, what did I think coming here would do?

59:06.125 --> 59:08.920
Oh, I'm such an idiot.

59:10.755 --> 59:13.675
He's been burned
on his face and neck.

59:15.134 --> 59:16.553
Thankfully, it's not severe.

59:16.636 --> 59:18.388
He won't need any kind of surgery,

59:18.471 --> 59:20.515
and I expect
he'll recover without scaring.

59:20.598 --> 59:22.725
What we're most concerned about
is possible injury

59:22.809 --> 59:24.310
to his left cornea from the explosion.

59:24.394 --> 59:27.021
We've done what we can
and only time will tell.

59:27.605 --> 59:29.107
His cornea got hit?

59:30.149 --> 59:34.028
That means he could lose
his eyesight, couldn't he, right?

59:34.112 --> 59:37.407
He responded well to the treatment,
so, well, it's not likely we'll--

59:37.490 --> 59:38.783
I don't care about that stuff.

59:40.535 --> 59:43.580
"The explosion damaged
his cornea severely."

59:44.080 --> 59:47.542
Could you tell them that?
Could you say that exactly in your report?

59:48.960 --> 59:52.505
My son should get
everything he's entitled to.

59:52.589 --> 59:55.842
What you say in that report is gonna,
it'll make or break us.

59:57.302 --> 59:59.637
Do you get what I need you to do?

01:00:00.972 --> 01:00:02.223
Well, I, uh…

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:33.546
You should have come alone
if you were worried.

01:00:34.756 --> 01:00:38.968
Si-woo's father
is hardly more than a parasite.

01:00:39.052 --> 01:00:40.178
He's got to go.

01:00:41.804 --> 01:00:44.599
Si-woo's cut him off a million times.

01:00:44.682 --> 01:00:47.560
Every time he tries, it doesn't last.

01:00:51.105 --> 01:00:52.940
Most people think you need your dad.

01:00:53.441 --> 01:00:55.943
For someone like Si-woo, though,
it's better being alone.

01:01:01.908 --> 01:01:03.785
Ah, Director Lady.

01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:06.954
There you are.

01:01:08.373 --> 01:01:09.832
So what's the deal?

01:01:13.544 --> 01:01:15.338
I was talking with that guy, the doctor.

01:01:17.131 --> 01:01:18.549
Si-woo could go blind.

01:01:20.510 --> 01:01:21.636
It's that bad?

01:01:21.719 --> 01:01:23.846
The explosion damaged the cornea.

01:01:23.930 --> 01:01:25.098
What do you think?

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:28.601
His whole life ahead taken away,
'cause he's blind.

01:01:30.019 --> 01:01:34.482
If you don't get him what he's due,
make it right, I'm gonna do something.

01:01:35.441 --> 01:01:38.569
Don't try and pull a fast one
and try to cheap us out.

01:01:38.653 --> 01:01:41.656
'Cause I'll tell the government
you're dirty.

01:01:41.739 --> 01:01:43.658
And I'll tell any reporters, too.

01:01:43.741 --> 01:01:45.076
Understand?

01:01:45.159 --> 01:01:47.704
If you make me do that…

01:01:49.122 --> 01:01:53.668
I'm gonna have to fire both you
and that guy, right?

01:01:54.544 --> 01:01:57.463
So don't think you can brush this
under the rug.

01:01:57.547 --> 01:02:00.633
Once you pay up, I'll go away.
Is that clear?

01:02:04.887 --> 01:02:06.556
I'm the person you should be talking to.

01:02:09.642 --> 01:02:11.436
Mind your own beeswax.

01:02:11.519 --> 01:02:13.604
Well, I'm a spokesperson for the KMA.

01:02:14.188 --> 01:02:16.441
This is my beeswax,
'cause I handle the press

01:02:16.524 --> 01:02:18.735
and relations with civilians.

01:02:18.818 --> 01:02:20.570
I came just to talk with you.

01:02:24.532 --> 01:02:26.409
- So let's talk.
- Damn it!

01:02:27.285 --> 01:02:28.578
Don't waste my time.

01:02:28.661 --> 01:02:30.621
You call up the head guy.

01:02:30.705 --> 01:02:33.708
Tell him to cut a check. Go. Go on.

01:02:34.208 --> 01:02:36.502
I don't have all day. Go call.

01:02:36.586 --> 01:02:39.505
Now that I've seen my boy,
we need no less than 30 mill, okay?

01:02:39.589 --> 01:02:40.590
Capisce?

01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:42.508
Don't waste any more of my time.

01:02:42.592 --> 01:02:44.552
- Make the call.
- That's enough!

01:02:45.094 --> 01:02:46.262
Huh?

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:48.181
Hey.

01:02:51.726 --> 01:02:54.103
- You're done.
- Hey. Wait, wait.

01:02:54.187 --> 01:02:56.939
Hang on. Wait, wait, wait. Idiot.

01:02:57.023 --> 01:02:59.150
Why aren't you lying in bed? Play it up.

01:02:59.233 --> 01:03:01.652
I can't believe you're walking.
You'll lose us money.

01:03:02.278 --> 01:03:05.490
- You're done.
- Come on, you're throwing it all away.

01:03:05.573 --> 01:03:06.866
I am.

01:03:06.949 --> 01:03:08.701
I'm ruining this chance for you.

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:09.952
- Aren't I?
- What?

01:03:10.036 --> 01:03:12.038
What charity will this money go to?

01:03:12.622 --> 01:03:14.791
Gambling? Scamming?

01:03:14.874 --> 01:03:15.833
Call girls?

01:03:15.917 --> 01:03:17.376
What do you need it for?

01:03:18.002 --> 01:03:20.296
- You little--
- You've always been a disgrace!

01:03:20.379 --> 01:03:22.048
You're an embarrassment.

01:03:23.883 --> 01:03:28.429
And the least you could do for me
is go and never show your face! Go!

01:03:28.513 --> 01:03:30.681
How dare you?

01:03:56.290 --> 01:03:57.542
That boy.

01:03:58.417 --> 01:03:59.460
Damn it.

01:04:04.715 --> 01:04:05.800
Make it right.

01:04:06.717 --> 01:04:08.135
Thirty million won.

01:04:09.262 --> 01:04:10.096
Thirty mill.

01:04:23.401 --> 01:04:24.986
So you came here to negotiate?

01:04:25.695 --> 01:04:27.822
- Huh?
- Did you?

01:04:30.241 --> 01:04:31.117
I did…

01:04:37.790 --> 01:04:38.916
Yu-jin.

01:04:58.394 --> 01:05:00.813
The 14th typhoon
of the season, Typhoon Ricky,

01:05:00.897 --> 01:05:03.733
is crossing the Korean peninsula
at a speed of 30m per hour.

01:05:06.527 --> 01:05:07.820
Hey, talk to me.

01:05:09.697 --> 01:05:11.574
Or I'll talk to you.

01:05:15.620 --> 01:05:19.332
It was a mistake for me
to bring your father, I'm sorry.

01:05:19.415 --> 01:05:20.917
- But--
- Some things

01:05:21.500 --> 01:05:23.252
aren't possible in this life.

01:05:25.212 --> 01:05:27.840
Like a person can never stop
a typhoon coming in.

01:05:29.175 --> 01:05:31.344
My dad isn't something you can change.

01:05:32.303 --> 01:05:33.971
That man will never…

01:05:35.222 --> 01:05:36.766
put in the work to change.

01:05:38.893 --> 01:05:40.895
I need to keep looking out for myself.

01:05:41.520 --> 01:05:43.397
I know you'll do the same thing, too.

01:05:48.945 --> 01:05:50.780
I've been thinking like you told me to.

01:05:53.574 --> 01:05:55.242
I thought about us every day.

01:05:59.580 --> 01:06:01.207
And I can't do what you want.

01:06:02.166 --> 01:06:04.085
I don't know what you're saying.

01:06:09.548 --> 01:06:13.386
The warm air in a typhoon
means it's incredibly altered

01:06:13.469 --> 01:06:16.639
when it encounters cool air
as happens when it hits Korea.

01:06:17.640 --> 01:06:21.519
We call it a variation area.

01:06:26.857 --> 01:06:28.317
I have to let you go.

01:06:29.944 --> 01:06:31.696
I can't stay moderate.

01:06:35.741 --> 01:06:37.868
Lee Si-woo,
has that typhoon warmth,

01:06:37.952 --> 01:06:40.454
when he met me, the cool air.

01:06:40.538 --> 01:06:46.002
Like a storm, he passed through,
and eventually had to say goodbye.

01:06:56.887 --> 01:06:57.930
Forgive me.

01:06:58.889 --> 01:07:00.224
I can't be what you want.

01:07:04.145 --> 01:07:05.354
So, let's…

01:07:08.983 --> 01:07:10.067
end it.

01:07:21.620 --> 01:07:23.080
How did we end up

01:07:23.998 --> 01:07:29.128
looking down a path with no idea
of what awaits us?

01:08:02.203 --> 01:08:04.080
Go back
to the hospital right now.

01:08:04.163 --> 01:08:06.540
I have no problem working.

01:08:06.624 --> 01:08:08.209
Is there a way for us to know sooner?

01:08:08.292 --> 01:08:09.919
We could launch a sonde
at the eastern side of Jeju

01:08:10.002 --> 01:08:11.462
and at the sea west of the island.

01:08:11.545 --> 01:08:13.339
But as you know,
it's too dangerous to go out

01:08:13.422 --> 01:08:16.092
into the sea in this weather
and to send out the sonde.

01:08:16.175 --> 01:08:17.259
We can only make predictions.

01:08:17.343 --> 01:08:20.221
There's no such thing
as an accurate forecast.

01:08:20.304 --> 01:08:22.181
Even if they're just predictions,

01:08:22.264 --> 01:08:23.891
I believe it is our duty to use

01:08:23.974 --> 01:08:26.435
the most accurate data possible
to make such predictions.

01:08:28.145 --> 01:08:30.356
You and I are married.
That's our conclusion.

01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:31.816
So tell me if you regret it.

01:08:31.899 --> 01:08:34.860
- Did you make my daughter cry?
- Sir, it's not what you think.

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:37.822
I don't think I can do this.

01:08:37.905 --> 01:08:39.240
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

01:08:39.323 --> 01:08:41.367
Let's break up, Si-woo.
